[{"id":"MaU_9","ref":"9","section":"Oṃ and its sound elements","sa":["जागरितस्थानो वैश्वानरोऽकारः प्रथमा मात्राऽऽप्तेरादिमत्त्वाद्","वाऽऽप्नोति ह वै सर्वान् कामानादिश्च भवति य एवं वेद ॥ ९॥"],"iast":["jāgaritasthāno vaiśvānaro’kāraḥ prathamā mātrā’’pterādimattvād","vā’’pnoti ha vai sarvān kāmānādiśca bhavati ya evaṃ veda ॥ 9॥"],"alt":[{"text":"The Waker, Vaiswanor, the Universal Male, He is A, the first letter, because of Initiality and Pervasiveness; he that knoweth Him for such pervadeth and attaineth all his desires; he becometh the source and first.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 195","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["जागरितस्थानः","jāgaritasthānaḥ","whose sphere is waking","jāgaritasthānaḥ"],["वैश्वानरः","vaiśvānaraḥ","Vaiśvānara","vaiśvānaraḥ"],["अकारः","akāraḥ","the sound A","akāraḥ"],["प्रथमा","prathamā","first","prathamā"],["मात्रा","mātrā","sound element","mātrā"],["आप्तेः","āpteḥ","because of attainment or pervasion","āpteḥ"],["आदिमत्त्वात्","ādimattvāt","because of being first","ādimattvāt"],["वा","vā","or","vā"],["आप्नोति","āpnoti","attains","√āp"],["ह","ha","indeed","ha"],["वै","vai","indeed","vai"],["सर्वान्","sarvān","all","sarvān"],["कामान्","kāmān","desires","kāmān"],["आदिः","ādiḥ","first","ādiḥ"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["भवति","bhavati","becomes","√bhū"],["यः","yaḥ","he who","yaḥ"],["एवम्","evam","thus","evam"],["वेद","veda","knows","√vid"]],"tr":{"text":"Vaisvanara seated in the waking state is the first letter a, owing to its all-pervasiveness or being the first. He who knows thus verily accomplishes all longings and becomes the first.","by":"Vidyavachaspati V. Panoli","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mandukyopanisad/5.9.mp3","whole":[187.17,211.71]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":10,"up":"mandukya"}]